## Phase 2: Private Artifact Registry Configuration

All internal SDKs—including `@enterprise/identity-sso`, `@enterprise/resilience-sdk`, and the `@enterprise/ui-tokens` design system—are published to private enterprise registries. Configure your package managers before building.

### 1. npm Registry Configuration (`.npmrc`)

Add the scoped registry URL and authentication token to your user home `~/.npmrc` or project-level `.npmrc`:

```ini
# Scope enterprise packages to private registry
@enterprise:registry=https://registry.enterprise.internal/repository/npm-hosted/
//registry.enterprise.internal/repository/npm-hosted/:_authToken=${ENTERPRISE_NPM_TOKEN}
always-auth=true
```

### 2. Android Gradle Registry Configuration (`settings.gradle.kts`)

Configure Gradle to authenticate with the internal Maven repository:

```kotlin
// settings.gradle.kts
dependencyResolutionManagement {
    repositoriesMode.set(RepositoriesMode.FAIL_ON_PROJECT_REPOS)
    repositories {
        google()
        mavenCentral()
        maven {
            url = uri("https://registry.enterprise.internal/repository/maven-releases/")
            credentials {
                username = System.getenv("ENTERPRISE_MAVEN_USER") ?: ""
                password = System.getenv("ENTERPRISE_MAVEN_TOKEN") ?: ""
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### 3. iOS CocoaPods Configuration (`Podfile`)

Point your project `Podfile` to the private Specs repository:

```ruby
# Podfile
platform :ios, '16.0'
use_frameworks!

# Public CocoaPods CDN
source 'https://cdn.cocoapods.org/'

# Enterprise Private Specs Repository
source 'git@github.enterprise.com:mobile-infra/cocoapods-specs.git'

target 'EnterpriseApp' do
  pod 'EnterpriseIdentity', '~> 2.4.0'
  pod 'EnterpriseResilience', '~> 1.8.0'
  pod 'DatadogRUM', '~> 2.12.0'
end
```

