## Top Enterprise Conventions & Best Practices

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">CRITICAL PRODUCTION CONVENTIONS</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Branch Naming Standard:</strong> Always use <code>feat/JIRA-1234-brief-name</code>, <code>fix/JIRA-1234-brief-name</code>, or <code>chore/brief-name</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>No Raw Secrets in Git:</strong> Never commit `.env` or keystore credentials. Credentials are injected dynamically by Bitrise secrets vault during CI runs.</li>
    <li><strong>Code Coverage Threshold:</strong> All new business logic in domain layers must maintain at least 80% unit test coverage.</li>
    <li><strong>Datadog Crash Triaging:</strong> All fatal crashes must have an assigned owner within 24 hours of notification in the mobile telemetry channel.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

